Four appliers under `patches/` rewrite files in the vLLM tree installed on
the serving box, at apply time, inside the container. The code those
appliers inject or edit is derived from Apache-2.0 vLLM-lineage modules and
remains under the Apache License 2.0 — see each file's own header:

- `patches/apply_sp_prefill.py` — injects the Apache-2.0-derived module
  `models/deepseek_v4/sp_prefill.py` (the injected module carries its
  upstream `SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0` header) and edits
  `models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py`,
  `model_executor/layers/vocab_parallel_embedding.py`,
  `model_executor/layers/fused_moe/runner/moe_runner.py`,
  `models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/ops/o_proj.py`,
  `models/deepseek_v4/attention.py` and
  `model_executor/layers/sparse_attn_indexer.py`
- `patches/apply_interactive_admission.py` — edits
  `vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py`
- `patches/apply_prefill_decode_interval.py` — edits
  `vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py`
- `patches/hotfix-dsv4-prefill-chunk-geospec.py` — edits
  `vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/indexer.py`

Every one of those edits is marker-guarded, idempotent and fail-closed, and
every edited file in the installed tree stays under its own upstream
license.

